    ],
    "summary": "Son of Blagger, the sequel to Blagger, is a scrolling platform game created by Tony Crowther and released by Alligata for the Commodore 64 computer in 1983. A ZX Spectrum port by Elliot Gay and a BBC Micro port were released in 1984.\nA clone of Son of Blagger was released for Amiga, titled Jonas Fulstrand. The game was released on a PD-Soft disk as Son of Blagger.\nA modern remake has been done for Windows with Game Maker Studio and a JavaScript version has been created with the help of the Phaser framework.",
    "developer": "Antony Crowther",
    "reviews": []
