      "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/512/5129201bba2cab7b6c21e1d5e326e25d.jpg",
      "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/6bb/6bb7bd7146f62c9c1b83401c2f2b5b12.jpg"
    ],
    "summary": "Granny's Garden is an educational adventure game for the British BBC Micro computer, released in 1983. It served as a first introduction to computers for many schoolchildren in the United Kingdom during the 1980s and 1990s. According to the 4Mation webpage about the original version, it was the reason many teachers decided that computers had a real place in education. The software is still available in its original and updated formats.\nCreated by Mike Matson for 4Mation, the game takes place in the Kingdom of the Mountains. The aim is to find the six missing children of the King and Queen (Esther, Tom, Clare, Anna, Jessica, and Daniel), while avoiding the evil witch, by solving puzzles.\nLet's Play videos have been published by fans of the game via YouTube.",
    "developer": "4Mation",
    "reviews": []
  },
