    ],
    "summary": "NATO Commander is a commercial computer strategy game designed by Sid Meier and released in 1983 by MicroProse. The game ran on 8-bit home computers of its day such as the Atari 8-bit family, Apple II and Commodore 64.\nThe player takes the role of the Supreme Allied Commander of NATO forces in Europe as they respond to a massive Warsaw Pact attack. The goal is to slow their advance and inflict casualties, hoping to force a diplomatic end to the war before West Germany is overrun.\nThe same game engine was also used as the basis for Conflict in Vietnam, Crusade in Europe and Decision in the Desert.",
    "developer": "MicroProse Software",
    "reviews": []
  },
