    ],
    "summary": "Shamus: Case II is a 1983 video game for the Atari 8-bit family written by William Mataga and published by Synapse Software. Mataga also wrote the original Shamus and the scrolling shooter Zeppelin. A port to the Commodore 64 by Joe Vierra was released in 1984.\nAlthough ostensibly a sequel to Shamus, the gameplay is very different, combining aspects of platformers, maze games, and even Breakout.\nCase II was as well received as the original, it did not inspire a Case III, and Synapse was soon insolvent.",
    "developer": "Synapse Software",
    "reviews": []
  },
