    ],
    "summary": "Atlantis is a fixed shooter video game released by Imagic in July 1982, for the Atari 2600. It was written by Dennis Koble who also wrote Trick Shot, Solar Storm, and Shootin Gallery' for Imagic. Atlantis was ported to the Atari 8-bit computers, Commodore VIC-20, Intellivision, and the Magnavox Odyssey².\nThe game was the subject of Destination Atlantis, a video game competition in which players of the Atari 2600 version were encouraged to mail in photos of their high scores to Imagic to receive a special edition of the game named Atlantis II.",
