      "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/fce/fceb7d5cb155de6722150eebb78d5ece.jpg",
      "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/917/917617669626fc9b1c846ef9afe03c60.jpg",
      "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/a0d/a0d538d9389e41499f449e8851846376.jpg",
      "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/fa5/fa5dbc330097aa72bf386abb9c7c988f.jpg"
    ],
    "summary": "Football Manager is a video game series published and developed by Addictive Games, the label set up by the game's creator Kevin Toms. The first game was released in 1982. It was then ported to most home computers during the 1980s and spawned several sequels: Football Manager 2 (1988) and Football Manager World Cup Edition (1990), both designed by Kevin Toms, and finally Football Manager 3 (1992), without Toms' involvement. Football Manager 3 sold poorly, and as a result the series came to an end. The series was claimed to have sold over a million copies by 1992. The game was to start a whole new genre of computer game, the football management simulation.",
    "developer": "Addictive Games",
    "reviews": []
  },
