      "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/593/593a8dfd505bdd7c99e0f2b2540d0d0b.jpg"
    ],
    "summary": "Demons to Diamonds is a fixed shooter for the Atari 2600 produced by Atari, Inc. and released in 1982. It was programmed by Nick Turner with graphics designed by Alan Murphy. Nick Turner previously ported Super Breakout to the 2600. The manual states that the game was \"primarily designed for children in the 6 to 12 age range.\"\nPlayers attempt to shoot demons in a \"cosmic carnival\" and then pick up the diamonds left behind by them, while dodging shots from enemy skulls. The game includes both single-player and two-player simultaneous play modes.",
    "developer": "Atari",
    "reviews": []
  },
