    ],
    "summary": "Cave of the Word Wizard is a 1982 educational children's game released for the Commodore 64 by Timeworks, Inc..\nThis is an educational game teaching spelling. The tuition is through spoken commands and dictated words for the player to spell. The player spells the words by typing on the keyboard and they are simultaneously displayed on the screen. The spoken commands and words are delivered in American English, through the computer audio output. Ten lists of words are provided for spelling, in graduated difficulty. You can also make custom lists. A list is selected at the start of each game.\nIt features a multilevel cave which the player's joystick guided character (selection of boy or girl) explores with the objective of finding a number of crystals in order to exit the dungeon. The charac",
    "developer": "Electronic Speech Systems",
    "reviews": []
